      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "This evaluates to: \\[\\begin{align*} \\dfrac{\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{7}{8}}{\\frac{4}{5}} &= \\dfrac{\\frac{5}{4}}{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\ &=\\left(\\dfrac{5}{4}\\right)^2 \\\\ &= \\dfrac{25}{16}.\\end{align*}\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Add the numerator fractions first.",
        "Dividing by \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) means multiplying by \\(\\frac{5}{4}.\\)"
      ],
